<section class="section" id="section-faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__header">
      <span class="section__label">FAQ</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 class="section__title">Dog Hoodie Manufacturer | Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div style="max-width: 800px;">
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          What fabric is best for a custom dog hoodie | French terry or fleece?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>French terry (220-300 GSM) is more breathable and holds its shape over repeated washes, making it better for mild climates or dogs that overheat easily. Fleece (280-360 GSM) traps more heat through its brushed nap, making it warmer for cold climates, but it pills faster and compresses over time. Most brands stock both | French terry for transitional seasons, fleece for deep winter.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          Should a dog hoodie have a harness hole?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>Yes, for any hoodie intended for daily walks. A harness hole placed at the harness D-ring's actual position during movement (not where it sits when the dog is standing still) lets the leash clip through without removing the hoodie. Poor placement causes the garment to twist, ripple, or slide off-centre as the dog moves and the leash pulls against misaligned fabric.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          What is the minimum order quantity for custom dog hoodies?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>300 pieces per style, split across sizes as needed. A different fabric (French terry vs fleece vs organic cotton) or a different cut counts as a separate style with its own 300-piece minimum. Multiple colourways of the identical pattern are usually treated as one style.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          Can dog hoodies be made from organic cotton?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>Yes. GOTS-certified organic cotton French terry or fleece is available, sourced and processed without synthetic pesticides or toxic dyes. Organic cotton hoodies typically cost more per unit than standard cotton-poly blends, and we'll quote both options side by side so you can compare before committing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          How long does dog hoodie sampling take?
